        <div class="fc-principles"><p><strong>Your course.</strong> Your configuration.</p><p><strong>Their repository.</strong> Their experiments.</p><p><strong>Fast feedback.</strong> More chances to learn.</p></div>

        <div class="fc-section" id="learner-flow">
          <div class="fc-section-heading"><p class="fc-eyebrow">A familiar workflow</p><h2>From assignment to insight.</h2><p>Keep the path into a programming exercise short, then let the student do the thinking.</p></div>
          <ol class="fc-flow">
            <li><span class="fc-step-number">01</span><h3>Accept</h3><p>Connect a GitHub account, confirm the course declaration, and receive a private copy of the assignment template.</p></li>
            <li><span class="fc-step-number">02</span><h3>Explore</h3><p>Open the project in a familiar Java environment. Read the question, inspect the tests, and turn an idea into an implementation.</p></li>
            <li><span class="fc-step-number">03</span><h3>Test</h3><p>Run JUnit locally and push changes. The shared GitHub action publishes feedback from the assignment's rubric and reports.</p></li>
            <li><span class="fc-step-number">04</span><h3>Improve</h3><p>Use failures as clues. Revise, test again, and discuss why the implementation behaves as it does.</p></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="fc-feature-band">
          <div><p class="fc-eyebrow">Built for the practical part</p><h2>Small exercises.<br /><em>Big questions.</em></h2></div>
          <div><p>Numerical methods and computational finance come alive when students can change a parameter, run an experiment, and test an assumption. A focused programming lab makes that exploration tangible.</p><p>Students can work with or without AI assistance, under the course's rules. The learning task remains the same: understand the method, examine the evidence, and explain the result.</p><p><a class="fc-text-link" href="motivation.html">Read the motivation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div>
        </div>

        <div class="fc-section fc-capabilities">
          <div class="fc-section-heading"><p class="fc-eyebrow">A clear scope</p><h2>Useful today.<br />Honest about what comes next.</h2></div>
          <div class="fc-capability-columns">
            <div class="fc-capability"><span class="fc-badge fc-badge-green">Available now</span><h3>Registration and feedback</h3><ul><li>GitHub sign-in and private template repositories</li><li>Student invitations and configured staff access</li><li>Maven/JUnit feedback and artifact collection</li><li>Local administration, SQLite history, and optional Moodle launches</li></ul></div>
            <div class="fc-capability fc-capability-future"><span class="fc-badge fc-badge-neutral">Still to build</span><h3>Submission and final grading</h3><ul><li>Automatic submission capture and source snapshots</li><li>An isolated runner with instructor-controlled tests</li><li>Authoritative final grades and Moodle grade return</li></ul><p>Student workflow results are learning feedback. They are not authoritative final grades.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fc-start-band"><div><p class="fc-eyebrow">Start with one exercise</p><h2>Take a look under the hood.</h2><p>One Java application, familiar tools, and an offline walkthrough before a live course pilot.</p></div><div class="fc-actions"><a class="fc-button fc-primary" href="https://github.com/finmath/finmath-classroom/blob/main/GETTING_STARTED.md">Open the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="fc-text-link" href="https://github.com/finmath/finmath-classroom">Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
      </div>
